# RELAYTO

- Public content on a site published with RELAYTO: its MCP server `https://<host>/mcp`
  (stdio: `npx -y relayto-mcp --site <host>`), its API via `npx relayto … --site <host>`,
  or `https://<host>/llms.txt` and each page's Markdown (`<page URL>.md`). No account.
  Content the publisher gated (private, password, email form, unlisted) is left out on
  purpose; don't try to reach it another way.
- A RELAYTO workspace the user belongs to: the RELAYTO MCP server,
  `https://mcp.relayto.com/mcp` (Streamable HTTP, OAuth sign-in). Stdio-only setups:
  `npx -y relayto-mcp`.
- Search before creating. Confirm privacy changes, removals, overwrites and invitations
  before calling the tool.
- Hub membership tools take ids (`objectID` in search results); settings, privacy,
  pages and analytics take slugs. Build links with `getUrlBySlug`.
- Never ask for a RELAYTO password; never write tokens to files.

Full instructions: AGENTS.md and the skills in `skills/`.
